    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nFor mappings/functions that operate on the cursors as a whole, the only way to stop cascading behavior is to guard the function with `nvim__mcursor_cascading()`. This affects jumps in follow mode (https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41995) and selection rotation (https://github.com/neovim/neovim/discussions/41928).\n\nIn the rotation discussion, clearing then restoring cursors was suggested as a workaround. But this would be more difficult if https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42004 were accepted. The appropriate cursors could be deleted and restored manually, but this creates the potential for error and comes with the performance cost inherent to setting extmarks (I'm not sure if that would even be faster than the is_cascading guard).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nN/A\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAn interface like this seems to make sense:\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_mcursor_nocascade(function()\n   -- Whatever the user wants to do\nend\n```\n\nThis would tie the nocascade behavior to the life of the Lua function execution (avoiding vim.schedule headaches). It also provides an additional simple anchor point to program around, hopefully reducing the need for carve-outs to the default behavior.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1684+g0ea627cfb7 Build type: Release LuaJIT 2.1.1788460057\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux Mint 22.1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.2.3\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\ntmux-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo\n\nEDIT: Apologies for mislabeling.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> But this would be more difficult if [#42004](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42004) were accepted.\n\nIf #42004 is implemented, it will set the `'` mark, so backtick-backtick can restore the primary if necessary.\n\n\n\n> This affects jumps in follow mode ([#41995](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41995))\n\n#41995 will be fixed.\n\nIs `nvim_mcursor_nocascade` needed if we have a way to enable/disable cascade (immediately, without `schedule()`) similar to `q=` ?",
